oindent Let $\vec{k} = [k]_1^N$ with $\omega(\vec{k}) = k$. Define its 'length' (from right, considering only entries larger than one) as $l(\vec{k}) = N+1-\min_{k_i > 1} \{i \}$. It easily follows from lemma ef{No_hole_strong_lemma} that if $F_N^{\vec{k}} 
eq 0$, we must have $l(\vec{k}) \leq \lceil  rac{k+3}{2} ceil - 1$. Therefore, according to lemma ef{zero_tail_lemma} we have :  egin{equation} F_N^{\vec{k}} = F_{\lceil  rac{k+3}{2} ceil}^{(k_{N-\lceil  rac{k+3}{2} ceil+1},\ldots,{k_N})} \end{equation} 
oindent for all $\vec{k}$'s in the sum. Summing on all $F_N^{\vec{k}}$ with the same 'weight', we get $C_N^{(k)} = C_{\lceil  rac{k+3}{2} ceil}^{(k)}, \quad  orall N > \lceil  rac{k+3}{2} ceil$. From the analyticity of $C_N$ and $ ar{H}$ around $\epsilon=0$, one can show by induction that $\lim_{N 	o \infty} C_N^{(k)} = C^{(k)}$, therefore we must have $C_N^{(k)} = C^{(k)}, \quad  orall N \geq \lceil  rac{k+3}{2} ceil $. \

Let $R = I + \epsilon T$. Assume that the entropy rate $ ar{H}$ is analytic in some neighborhood of $\delta = 0$. Then $ ar{H}$ satisfies : $$  ar{H} = -\pi^t [M .* \log M] \xi + \xi^t \Bigl\{ diag(\log (\pi)) T^t diag(\pi) M - $$  egin{equation} [diag(\pi) M T + T^t diag(\pi) M] .* [\log(diag(\pi) M)] \Bigr\} \xi \epsilon + O(\epsilon^2) \end{equation}  egin{proof} Noting that according to Thm. ef{high_SNR_thm}, $ ar{H} = C_2 + O(\epsilon^2)$, we first compute (exactly) $C_2$, and then expand it by substituting $R = I + \epsilon T$. Write $C_2$ as : $$ C_2 = H(Y_N | Y_{N-1}) = $$  egin{equation} -\sum_{i,j} P(Y_N = j, Y_{N-1} = i) \log  rac{P(Y_N = j, Y_{N-1} = i)}{P(Y_{N-1}=i)} \end{equation} 
oindent We can express the above probabilities as : $$ P(Y_{N-1}=i) = [\pi R]_i $$  egin{equation} P(Y_N = j, Y_{N-1} = i) = [R^t diag(\pi) M R]_{ij} \equiv F_{ij} \end{equation} 
oindent Substituting eq. (ef{prob_ys_eqs}) in eq. (ef{C_2_eq}), and writing in matrix form, we get :  egin{equation} C_2 = \Bigl\{ [log(\pi R)] F - \xi^T [F .* log F] \Bigr\} \xi \end{equation} 
oindent Substituting $R = I + \epsilon T$ gives : $$ F = diag(\pi) M + [diag(\pi) M T + T^t diag(\pi) M] \epsilon + O(\epsilon^2), $$ $$ F .* \log F = [diag(\pi) M] .* \log(diag(\pi) M) + $$ $$ \Bigl\{[diag(\pi) M T + T^t diag(\pi) M] .* [I + \log(diag(\pi) M)]\Bigr\} \epsilon + $$  egin{equation} O(\epsilon^2) \end{equation} 
oindent Substituting these in eq. (ef{general_alphabet_ hmm_entropy}) gives, after simplification, the result (ef{general_1st_order_final}). \end{proof}

